---
name: review-task
version: 1.0.0
description: lead phase-ending code review template for codex-orchestration phases.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - phase
  - branch
  - commit
  - worktree_path
  - review_focus
  - review_questions
  - references
optional_variables:
  - lead
  - cc
defaults:
  lead: team-lead
  cc: team-lead
metadata:
  type: review-task
  tags:
    - stage:review
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: phase
      variable: phase
    state: review-start
    stage: review
    transition: start
---
{#- Temporary workaround for sc-compose #784: v1.7.0 rejects autoescape blocks. Revert these | safe filters once a release containing #788 is pinned. -#}
<atm-review id="{{ task_id | safe }}" phase="{{ phase | safe }}">
  <description>Phase-ending code review. Read-only analysis only; no code changes.</description>

  <branch>{{ branch | safe }}</branch>
  <commit>{{ commit | safe }}</commit>
  <worktree>{{ worktree_path | safe }}</worktree>

  <review-focus>
{{ review_focus | safe }}
  </review-focus>

  <review-questions>
{{ review_questions | safe }}
  </review-questions>

  <references>
{{ references | safe }}
  </references>

  <output-format>
    Structured findings report with sections:
    1. SUMMARY — one-paragraph verdict
    2. FINDINGS — numbered list, each with severity, location, finding, recommendation
    3. EXTRACTION-READINESS — score 1-5 per relevant module with rationale
    4. RECOMMENDED-NEXT-SPRINTS — concrete follow-up work items
  </output-format>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a">Start the task immediately with `atm task start {{ task_id | safe }} "<one line: what you will do first>"`, then begin the review in the same work session.</step>
    <step id="b">Read the relevant source and doc files in the specified worktree and commit context.</step>
    <step id="c">Do not make any code changes.</step>
    <step id="d">Deliver the structured findings report by closing the task with the report as the body: `atm task close {{ task_id | safe }} completed --stdin <<'EOF' … EOF`. Only this close frees your queue: the next assignment stays queued and never starts until `{{ task_id | safe }}` is closed, and a plain `atm send` report does not close it. Re-verify every cited file:line against the current branch and worktree before reporting it; stale or missing evidence is a finding, not a guess. {% if cc and cc != lead %}Copy a one-line summary to `{{ cc | safe }}` with a plain `atm send {{ cc | safe }} --stdin`.{% endif %}</step>
  </workflow>
</atm-review>
{#- end of sc-compose #784 workaround -#}
